> First, I played level one unpatched. Went to save and got this on my screen:
> http://i.imgur.com/xU6YTOm.png
> When I started my game again, everything was saved. What's going on here?

I think the game first saved your character successfully, then tried to
compress the save file and the compressing failed.
Check the definiton of COMPRESS in include/config.h, maybe it points to
something that doesn't exist in your system in the place defined.
(Mine points to /usr/bin/compress which is the default location.)
When you restored, the game found the file that was not compressed.

> Next, I went to edit .nethackrc and found it to be empty. Is it supposed
> to be empty? I'm used to compiling, patching, and playing under Windows.

The file doesn't exist in your home directory before you create it or
copy from elsewhere.
An example can be found in the source tree as sys/share/NetHack.cnf.
You can copy it as .nethackrc in your home directory to begin with.
Remember to set the permissions so that the game can read it.
chmod a+x ~
chmod a+r ~/.nethackrc
(I think that will do.)

